  "onboardingWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to Glide",
  "onboardingWelcomeBody": "Glide uses your phone's camera to warn you about obstacles ahead, reads signs and text aloud, and guides you back to places you save. Everything happens on your phone, and it works without an internet connection.",
  "onboardingSafetyTitle": "Glide is an extra aid",
  "onboardingSafetyBody": "Glide can miss things. It does not see every obstacle, it cannot see holes or drop-offs reliably, and it can never tell you that it is safe to cross a road. Keep using your cane, guide dog and judgement. Glide is there to add information, not to replace them.",
  "onboardingHoldTitle": "Hold the phone upright",
  "onboardingHoldBody": "Hold the phone at chest height, screen towards you and the back camera facing the way you walk, or use a chest harness. The screen stays on while Glide is watching or guiding, which uses more battery.",
  "onboardingFeelTitle": "Learn the vibrations",
  "onboardingFeelBody": "One pulse means an obstacle further away. Two pulses mean it is within 3 metres. A fast burst means it is very close. Three long pulses mean there may be a street crossing ahead. Try them now.",
  "onboardingCrossingPattern": "possible street crossing",
  "onboardingPrivacyTitle": "Your privacy",
  "onboardingPrivacyBody": "Camera images never leave your phone and are not saved. Your location is used only while you navigate, and the only places stored are the ones you save. You can delete everything in Settings, under Delete my data.",
